			"widgets_values":[
				"Visual:\nAn absurd but photorealistic vertical vlog featuring a stern ancient Chinese imperial guard inside a modern 24-hour self-service laundromat at midnight. He wears a dark red embroidered robe, a black winged official hat, leather wrist guards, and a sheathed sword at his waist. His posture is disciplined, his expression is severe, and he behaves as though he is carrying out an important imperial mission.\n\nThe laundromat is ordinary and brightly lit, with rows of front-loading washing machines, plastic laundry baskets, detergent vending machines, handwritten notices, and several sleepy customers in casual clothes. The serious historical character creates a strong comedic contrast with the mundane modern environment.\n\n[Shot 1]\nThe imperial guard records himself with a smartphone held at arm’s length while walking slowly past the washing machines. His sword sheath lightly taps against his robe as he moves.\n\nHe looks directly into the phone camera and reports in a deep, formal Mandarin voice:\n\n“子时已到，奉命清洗战袍。”\n\nBehind him, several washing machines rotate steadily. One customer pauses while folding clothes and looks at him in confusion.\n\n[Shot 2] 3.2s\nHe turns the phone camera toward a washing machine filled with dark red robes spinning rapidly behind the glass door.\n\nHe points at the machine with complete seriousness and says:\n\n“此乃西域机关，水攻、旋击，一气呵成。”\n\nThe washing machine suddenly enters a faster spin cycle. He instinctively steps back and places one hand on the sword handle, watching the machine with suspicion.\n\n[Shot 3] 6.4s\nThe camera returns to selfie framing. He slowly relaxes, removes his hand from the sword, and gives a restrained approving nod.\n\nA tired laundromat employee asks from outside the frame:\n\n“先生，要加柔顺剂吗？”\n\nThe guard turns toward the employee and replies solemnly:\n\n“加。明日面圣，衣袍不可失礼。”\n\nHe looks back into the camera, lowers his voice, and concludes:\n\n“此地办事，甚是利落。”\n\nAt the final moment, a washing-machine completion chime sounds. He immediately stands upright as though receiving an imperial order.\n\nCamera:\nVertical first-person smartphone vlog recorded by the imperial guard himself. Use one continuous handheld take with mild natural arm movement, slightly imperfect selfie framing, realistic autofocus transitions between his face and the washing-machine window, subtle exposure changes under cold fluorescent lighting, and mild wide-angle smartphone-lens distortion.\n\nEvery action must follow clear physical causality: he walks past the machines, turns the phone toward the spinning clothes, reacts to the faster spin cycle, reaches toward his sword, recognizes there is no danger, relaxes, responds to the employee, and reacts to the completion chime.\n\nPreserve the guard’s facial identity, hat, robe, sword position, smartphone, laundromat layout, washing-machine contents, and employee position throughout. Avoid costume changes, historical scenery appearing inside the laundromat, magical effects, exaggerated martial-arts movement, duplicate limbs, distorted hands, floating objects, rapid cuts, smooth commercial camera movement, or cartoon physics.\n\nAudio:\nSpoken language is Mandarin Chinese. The imperial guard has a deep adult male voice with formal, restrained, and completely serious delivery. The laundromat employee has a tired young adult female voice from outside the frame.\n\nPreserve all dialogue verbatim with clear turn-taking and accurate lip synchronization. Include realistic laundromat ambience: washing-machine motors, water movement, spin-cycle vibration, fluorescent electrical hum, plastic basket contact, distant clothes folding, the sword sheath lightly touching fabric, and a clear washing-machine completion chime near the end.\n\nNo background music, no subtitles, and no on-screen text.",
